	I second the recommendation for Understanding DCE.  It is a nice
once-over by some very knowledgable people.  It doesn't go into any
details, though, so you might want also to buy the Guide to Writing DCE
Applications, in the same O'Reilly series.  It actually only convers
writing DCE RPC applications (no real coverage of naming, threads, or
security), but it's still quite useful.  Regarding comparison of DCE and
Sun ONC I don't know of any currently published books on the subject,
but I will be presenting such a comparison at two upcoming conferences:
the Silicon Valley Networking Conference April 12-14 in Santa Clara,
California, and the OSF DCE Workshop in Karlsruhe, Germany, October 7-8.
You might consider attending the latter, as it is in your neck of the
woods so to speak.  Regards,

