I've administered a DEC 3000/500 Alpha workstation for at least 9 months, both
under OpenVMS and OSF/1.  DEC's OSF/1 is fine.  Only a few minor differences
from other flavors of unix.  Usenet software ports easily.  Damn fast X
windows!!!  As far as that goes, a damned fast system.

The only real complaint I have is that DEC doesn't support OS upgrades.  To
upgrade the OS, you actually have to reinstall and reconfigure from scratch
(just like SunOS).  Sure makes it hard to customize and localize a system when
you have to do it over and over with every new release.

One last comment.  I hate ALL license managers.  It's too bad, but we
apparently will HAVE to learn to live with them.  At least with DEC's, once you
finally GET all the PAKs you need, it's plug and play.  So far, we haven't had
all the hassles that we get with other vendors daemons.  Then again, I only
have the one Alpha, so haven't tried using floating network licenses.

--

        Patrick Wolfe (pwolfe@kai.com, uunet!kailand!pwolfe)
        Sr. System Manager, Kuck & Associates



